<h3>KNOMI</h3>
<p>Status for the KNOMI display. Over WiFi the KNOMI reads it from the API. Over Bluetooth this plugin pushes it.</p>

<form class="form-horizontal" onsubmit="return false;">
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Tool</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-small" data-bind="value: settings.settings.plugins.knomi.tool">
      <span class="help-block">Temperature shown on the KNOMI over Bluetooth (usually tool0).</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <legend>Bluetooth</legend>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" data-bind="checked: settings.settings.plugins.knomi.ble_enabled"> Connect to the KNOMI over Bluetooth
      </label>
      <span class="help-block">
        Turn Bluetooth on for the KNOMI on its own settings page first, then pair once from the Pi:
        <code>bluetoothctl</code>, <code>scan on</code>, <code>pair &lt;KNOMI address&gt;</code>, type the code the KNOMI shows,
        then <code>trust &lt;address&gt;</code>.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">KNOMI address</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <input type="text" class="input-medium" placeholder="auto" data-bind="value: settings.settings.plugins.knomi.ble_address">
      <span class="help-block">Leave empty to find it automatically. It's filled in after the first connection.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <label class="control-label">Status</label>
    <div class="controls">
      <span data-bind="text: bleState"></span>
      <button class="btn btn-mini" data-bind="click: refresh">Refresh</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="control-group">
    <div class="controls">
      <button class="btn" data-bind="click: wifiOn">Turn KNOMI WiFi on</button>
      <span class="help-block">If the KNOMI turned its WiFi off for Bluetooth, this brings WiFi back for 10 minutes (e.g. to open its web page).</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</form>
